# Newly introduced migrations require an ARM review before they can run.
# Format: migration filename<TAB>run|skip<TAB>exact SHA-256<TAB>review rationale
# A skip entry must document why the migration is Pi-inapplicable.  Missing or
# stale entries stop the package transaction before it starts.
# A run entry executes as the detached desktop user, with no interactive
# terminal or sudo prompt/keepalive guaranteed. It must be noninteractive and
# desktop-user compatible. Privileged work requires a separately reviewed
# updater implementation; an allowlist entry alone does not grant it.
